{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/255148-resources-for-changeling-history","id":255148,"title":"Resources for Changeling History","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-12T02:49:46-07:00","id":255148,"title":"Resources for Changeling History","content":"So a friend and I were throwing ideas around for a historian Changeling character and then came the paradox (small P) of the fact that Dreams and Fae spirits themselves exists outside of Time. History can only be chronicled pertaining to events that occur on earth. Even Changeling minds and Memories don't exactly fall in any Linear way. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So I'm asking how you might have handled History in your Dreaming Changeling universe. Is it laid out in a quasi timeline of events? Or does everything start with Once Upon a Time? <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The books treat Fae history in a sort of Vague way mentioning events surrounding a period in human history, but that's still anchored in the Human world. While other events purely related to the Dream world and Arcadia are labeled Time Immemorial. Maybe I'm overthinking it and being too analytical in looking for accuracy in a game like Changeling, but I'm really interested in trying to explore this character concept in a Changeling. Vampire has their Beckett and Werewolf has their Death-Takes-Last. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This also ties in to a writing project I wanted to try, but I'll need your help and Ideas about the Fae's perception and recording of Time and stories before I can work on that project. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks. Peace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T10:01:13-07:00","id":255370,"title":"","content":"I found that Changeling history is a combination of quasi-timeline and Once Upon a Time. It has parallels to Garou history, primarily oral and is usually determined by who is telling the history. While a lot of the history takes place in prehistory and/or Biblical times, it gets obscured or combined with the Medieval setting so your not quite sure if they are talking about prehistory or after the fall of Rome. There are set timeline events, even with the Medieval mixup you have a approximate time and date. The dates are The Sundering (the beginning of myth and legend, somewhere in prehistory when magic starts failing for Mages), the rumors of Tir-na-Nog (the aftermath of The Sundering, which are the Americas aka The Summer Lands, Ireland and parts of the British Isles still have connection to the Dreaming), The Age of Travel (about the same time and age as the Roman Empire), The Shattering (either the second or third Maelstrom, Medieval times from the Black Plague to the beginning of the Renaissance), the Shattering is what Changelings remember the most and keep using the style of the time for recalling their earlier history), Interregnum (my guess during the Renaissance, when commoner Changelings started to become authority figures when the Sidhe bailed), The Concord (Renaissance to 1960s-ish, when all the modern Changeling troupes/archetypes/law was established) The Accordance War (1969-1971, the only solid timeline date also known as the Changeling &quot;Civil War&quot;, and during that The Rise of High King David, the laws/traditions gets reorganized for modern times bringing in commoner rights), and now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T16:30:55-07:00","id":256355,"title":"","content":"Prehistory - Arcadia and/or Dreaming is at it's strongest, cohesides with Mage Prehistory and maybe Garou history as well. The start of Myth and Legend.<br /> The Sundering - Either the Flood or the Tower of Babel triggering the separation from the Dreaming and the Real World, Biblical disasters start separating the Changelings, afterwards rumors of a kingdom called Tir-Na-Nog starts to be milled.<br /> The Age of Travel - Roman Empire (ish); Changelings use Roman roads and trade routes to find trods and the Silver Gate, trods are contested as Banality gets stronger from Roman engineering and sciences. Movies; Centurion, Gladiator. Shows; Rome, Spartacus.<br /> The Shattering - Black Plague to start of Renaissance; triggered by the Second Maelstrom, Banality is at it's worse as despair and gloom take a hold of the mortals, the Sidhe noble and others flee to Arcadia as the trods become lost, commoners left behind attempt to rebuild, it is rumored that the Shattering became the default style for historical reference. Movies; Adventures of Robin Hood, Willow, Kingdom of Heaven. Specials; The Black Plague. Anime; Basilisk.<br /> Interregun - Renaissance; Commoners continue rebuilding using Feudalism as their governing system, Commoner Nobles rise as freeholds established, possibly the start of an official written record. Movies; The Da Vinci Code.<br /> Concord - Post Renaissance? to 1969; As Seelie and Unseelie courts rise no official treaties until the Concord was struck, neither side will trespass on each others territory, and was the longest lasting peace treaty until the lunar landing.<br /> The Accordance War - 1969 to 1971; The lunar landing reignites the imagination and opens trods, bringing the Nobility back to the world, old servants return to their masters' sides as the attempt to being their old laws back to the modern world, war breaks out with Commoners and Nobles fight over the rights of Commoners, the war in America sweeps from the Californian coast to the Eastern Sea Board with Nobility victory after another. High King David fights in the war and wins both the hearts of Nobility and the Commonwealth, ending the war and modernizing the system. Movies; The Warriors.<br /> <br /> Also, the reason why Changeling history is distorted is to prevent Banality. Which is why when Changelings talk about anything before the Shattering it is blurred with the Medieval style (weapons, clothing, mannerisms) but the events are still told as if from old legends or Biblical stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T18:22:02-07:00","id":256408,"title":"","content":"Wow thank you Paladin Demo.<br /> <br /> I was trying to crawl through my Changeling books to make a list like this myself after yer last post, but I only got as far as picking out the events up to and around the Shattering.<br /> <br /> I'm probabaly making it too big and hard for myself, I was also trying to factor in the other things like when the Summer court took over and what the other Thallain must have been up to and where does Denizens fit in and don't get me started on Land of 8 Million Dreams.<br /> <br /> When you say Biblical, what do you mean exactly? Like what examples? Bible Era of spreading Christianity? or the reputed history of the world depicted in biblical events? I don't know which the World of Darkness runs on, but I'm trying to keep it religion neutral so as not to offend anyone. The History of how Christianity spread and the History the Bible says happened are distinctly different so I just wanna make sure which one you are referring to. Having something be Biblical is also an expression meaning Huge (&quot;A swarm of Biblical proportions!&quot;) So do you mean Biblical disasters such a Huge disasters or the actual 10 Biblical Plagues and The Flood or The Smiting of Sodom and Gamorra? etc?<br /> <br /> There's also the subject of referencing Garou and Mage Prehistory since Changeling history has the opinion that Garou as well Magi are divergent branches of Fae linage that everyone's forgotten the where and when that happened.<br /> <br /> Again, maybe I'm over complicating this, but I think it'd be fun and enjoyable to defvelop a framework for a historian character for Changeling, especially with the suggestion that they avoid history for reasons of Banality. One Fae's Banaity can be another Fae's Passion. Thank you again for the advice and suggestions. I look forward to your answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T19:17:15-07:00","id":256424,"title":"","content":"Try cyclical time with events tied to the transit of Neptune through the zodiac a cycle that repeats at roughly 164 years. Thus events from 2011 to 2024 roughly mirror those of 1847 to 1860, from 1683 to 1696, and from 1519 to 1532. Changeling outfits would tend to mimic these earlier time periods and their politics would tend to reenact those earlier times. Figure a 25% loss of influence between each cycle. Thus the 1847-1860 cycle would only have a 75% chance of influencing contemporary events, the 1683-1696 cycle would be only 56.25% effective and the 1519-1532 cycle would only be 42.19% influential on the present. Of course since the dreaming isn't bound by time events in the present have an equivelent chance of influencing the past. Likewise we have the same chance of being influenced by and influencing the future. 2175-2188 would have a 75% chance of influencing contemporary events; 2339-2352 would have a 56.25% chance; 2503-2516 would have a 42.19% impact; 2667-2680 would have a 31.64% impact; 2831-2844 would touch us at 223.73% and 2995-3008 would affect us at only 17.8%; beyond that the cycles would be pretty much lost to background noise. <br /> <br /> Since arts and music are important to changelings look for theater revivals of plays from the earlier periods along with movie adaptations. Best selling novels from these earlier cycles will also be adapted into movies with music from these periods finding it's way into motion picture soundtracks and videogames.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T13:44:12-07:00","id":256808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/255148-resources-for-changeling-history?p=256408#post256408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow thank you Paladin Demo.<br /> <br /> I was trying to crawl through my Changeling books to make a list like this myself after yer last post, but I only got as far as picking out the events up to and around the Shattering.<br /> <br /> I'm probabaly making it too big and hard for myself, I was also trying to factor in the other things like when the Summer court took over and what the other Thallain must have been up to and where does Denizens fit in and don't get me started on Land of 8 Million Dreams.<br /> <br /> When you say Biblical, what do you mean exactly? Like what examples? Bible Era of spreading Christianity? or the reputed history of the world depicted in biblical events? I don't know which the World of Darkness runs on, but I'm trying to keep it religion neutral so as not to offend anyone. The History of how Christianity spread and the History the Bible says happened are distinctly different so I just wanna make sure which one you are referring to. Having something be Biblical is also an expression meaning Huge (&quot;A swarm of Biblical proportions!&quot;) So do you mean Biblical disasters such a Huge disasters or the actual 10 Biblical Plagues and The Flood or The Smiting of Sodom and Gamorra? etc?<br /> <br /> There's also the subject of referencing Garou and Mage Prehistory since Changeling history has the opinion that Garou as well Magi are divergent branches of Fae linage that everyone's forgotten the where and when that happened.<br /> <br /> Again, maybe I'm over complicating this, but I think it'd be fun and enjoyable to defvelop a framework for a historian character for Changeling, especially with the suggestion that they avoid history for reasons of Banality. One Fae's Banaity can be another Fae's Passion. Thank you again for the advice and suggestions. I look forward to your answers.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem. Recently lost my job, and after my first job hunt decided to occupy my time. Don't have any of the sidebooks, so I figured just use what's in the corebook to establish a baseline. Anything from the sidebooks you can tack on where it falls into the timeline. Now addressing your concerns.<br /> <br /> I was going off the reputed history. Vampire the Masquerade has the Flood (which is also referenced in the Rokea Breedbook) as it's defining Biblical distaster. When I was thinking of what disaster between the Flood and the Plagues, from what the book described it sounded similar to the Tower of Babel disaster (the one where the king tried to challenge God and God decided to split his kingdom by dividing the citizens). How it was written Changelings were one in the same until the Sundering separated the Dreaming from the Real World, dividing the Changelings as well. Other disasters like Sodom and Gamorrah would have been the first Unseelie settlements getting raised by Seelie magic.<br /> <br /> Each of the Supernaturals' histories interconnect with one another in some form or another, most just reference that the other exist and use to be their own. I should have wrote in possibly cohesided with Garou and Magi history since before the Sundering that was when Gaia and Magic in that time was the strongest. It might have been the Sundering that branched the Garou, Magi, and others from Changelings, or at least what the Changelings might believe since their records aren't quite clear to begin with.<br /> <br /> My extra tidbit with how they tell their history to avoid Banality, pretty much their official written records started at Interregun, anything pre-Shattering would be oral history so it's highly influenced by the one who is telling the story. Also why I suspected that Changeling history is Once Upon a Time as well as a quasi-timeline. Something to avoid Childer gaining Banality earily while the older Seemings would be mroe used to Banality and can delve into history without much recourse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T09:48:46-07:00","id":261320,"title":"","content":"Exert for your historian.<br /> <br /> <i>There is nothing more thrilling than a good challenge, and there is nothing more challenging than decoding our own history. It is strange history indeed. While there some correlations to historical texts, but our history is a blend of the factual and the fantastical. I have a theory for that, while there are historical records kept by our Kithain, our history is not only an oral history but it is told in such a way that our Fledges and Childer can avoid early exposure to Banality. With Wylder such as myself and most notibally Grumps, we can delve into our history without much recourse, how can Banality take hold when we are use to it's effects. There is another theory from a fellow historian that the notable time periods coincide with the orbit of Neptune, some of the timeline but from what I observed there are huge gaps between dates and other events of the timeline such as The Concord have extended periods than others like The Shattering. Speaking of, one of my theories that The Shattering is the Kithains' version of the dramatic events of 9/11, an even so traumatizing that everything has been affected by it. Our mannerisms, our systems, even our history has been affected by The Shattering. Honestly, I can understand why, the Plague is a terrible time; the death, despair, the Banality, it must have been hard to be Kithain during the Shattering. Fortunatly, I will assist you with our history and where it falls in the mortal timeline. Where shall we begin?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}